# CHANAKYA Radar (CO-SPRINT-105)

## First-viewport principle (mandatory)

Every pixel on the first visible screen must help answer:

> **What should I work on right now?**

Anything else moves to the global header, inside the Radar container, or below the fold.

## Page hierarchy

1. Global header (EUX-007)
2. Radar header (title · count · scope · Direction/Concern/Trend)
3. Radar visual
4. Scrollable analytics / KPIs

No separate ticker row. No dedicated Team/scope row outside the Radar.

## Global header (Mission Control)

`Rupee Catalyst` · `ChanakyaLiveIntelligenceBar` · Notifications · Radar|Kanban · CHANAKYA AI · User Profile

No search field. No extra controls below the header.

## Radar container

- Row 1: `Operational Radar · N Active Deals` + scope select (top-right)
- Row 2: `Direction | Concern | Trend`
- Visual begins immediately below that header

## Architecture

- Deal Workspace is the click target from Radar points / status rows (not Opportunity Workspace)
- Opportunity Preview may remain as secondary sheet chrome; never permanently shrinks Radar
## CO-SPRINT-108 — Daily Work Completion Indicator

- **Business Status** = dot colour (quadrant). Independent of daily work.
- **Daily Work ✓** = meaningful Operational Work on the **current business day** only.
- Config: `CHANAKYA_RADAR_MEANINGFUL_WORK_ACTIVITIES` + `CHANAKYA_RADAR_NON_OPERATIONAL_ACTIVITY_PATTERNS`.
- SSOT: `hasMeaningfulWorkToday` / `recordChanakyaRadarOperationalWork` in `daily-work.ts`.
- Opening or viewing a file must **never** set ✓.
- New business day automatically clears ✓ (day-keyed marks; status/stage/ageing unchanged).

- **Ring model** (`CHANAKYA_RADAR_AGEING_RINGS`): distance from centre = stage ageing (config thresholds, not hardcoded UI).
- Placement: `placeChanakyaRadarBlips` — angular spacing + collision avoid within ring; small radial jitter; no continuous arcs.
- **Operational Vector** (green needle): living management-attention bearing (`attentionWeight`); not decorative.
- **Operational Vector — BUSINESS CERTIFIED** (logic · math · behaviour · production readiness). Approved for production. No refactor required for current release.
- **Future platform hardening (scheduled separately):** evolve to a visualization-independent contract — Enterprise Attention Score · Highest Attention Quadrant · Confidence — with Radar as a presentation adapter only. Coupling to 0°/90°/180°/270° is acceptable now; not a certification blocker.
- Quadrant fills/borders are context only — dots are primary.
- No redundant colour legends under the Radar.
- Ticker is passive; detail via CHANAKYA AI only
- Page must naturally scroll
- Metric SSOT / Vector / Health — never reimplemented in UI
- Real-time: `subscribeLoanFilesUpdated` + 60s / `storage` fallback
- Matrix retired; Kanban cards never draggable
- Quadrants: On Track (N) · Follow-up Required (E) · At Risk (S) · Needs Attention (W)

## CO-MC-001 — Enterprise Activity Intelligence

CHANAKYA Radar v2.0 calculation enhancement (UI frozen — dial unchanged).

- **Engine SSOT:** `src/lib/enterprise-activity-intelligence/`
- **Config:** `src/constants/enterprise-activity-intelligence/`
- **Types:** `src/types/enterprise-activity-intelligence.ts`
- Meaningful activities reuse `CHANAKYA_RADAR_MEANINGFUL_WORK_ACTIVITIES` + non-operational exclusions (view/open never counts).
- Every active Deal gets an **Activity Momentum Score** and **Transaction Activity State**:
  Active Today · Recently Active · Healthy Waiting · Needs Follow-up · At Risk.
- **Healthy Waiting** (within expected lender/legal/ops/customer TAT) must **not** reduce Radar classification or Deal Health.
- Momentum blends into Deal Health and Operational Vector attention / Trend via `classifyOperationalDeal` + `buildChanakyaRadarDashboard`.
- Do not reimplement Activity Momentum in UI, Mission Control, or EBI — consume Radar / Activity Intelligence SSOT only.

## CO-CHANAKYA-RADAR-003 — Enterprise Deal Radar

CHANAKYA Radar is the **Executive Operational Deal Radar** — Active Deals only (not customers / opportunities).

### Active Deals only

Exclude Lost · Disbursed · Cancelled · Withdrawn · Archived (and terminal lender books). Terminal Deals must never appear on the dial, status cards, Average Deal Health, or CHANAKYA operational analytics.

SSOT filter: `isLiveActiveLoanFile` / `listActiveRadarDealFiles`.

### Decision Engine

Multi-parameter classification (`classifyOperationalDeal`) — not a single Health Score gate.

Signals include stage / sub-stage, ageing, tasks, documents, SLA / delay, blockers.

Categories: On Track · Needs Attention · Follow-up Required · At Risk.

Thresholds: `CHANAKYA_RADAR_CLASSIFICATION_THRESHOLDS` (configurable SSOT — no UI hardcoding).

### Layout

- Radar dial is the hero — nothing overlaps it; generous breathing space.
- Four outside premium glass status cards (~25% denser than prior feeds):
  - Top Left — ON TRACK
  - Top Right — FOLLOW-UP REQUIRED
  - Bottom Left — NEEDS ATTENTION
  - Bottom Right — AT RISK
- Continuous bottom→top auto-scroll; no scrollbar; no manual scroll.
- Rows: Deal Reference · Customer · Product · Lender · Current Stage.
- Hover (point or row): Deal Ref · Customer · Product · Lender · Stage · Sub Stage · Days in Stage · Deal Health · Classification · Reason · CHANAKYA Recommendation.
- Click point or row → Deal Workspace (`buildDealWorkspaceHref`).
- Centre score = **Average Deal Health** (mean of active-deal health scores only).

UI: `radar-status-scroll-card.tsx` · `chanakya-radar-visual.tsx`

